  {
    "episode_id": 96797,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96797.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, first off, you get a lot of things brought to you that you didn't, you know, you didn't anticipate. But I really do think that the most important thing is to continue what we've been doing. As you know, when I got elected back in 2010, the state was in trouble financially. We do more people leaving the state than moving in. We're able to turn the economy around. And what I appreciate is that, you know, Tallahassee is continuing to work on that. So, but, you know, some things get brought to you based on, you know, things happening at the time. So, the, but what I'm glad about is, you know, we're still focused on keeping our taxes low, keeping our economy going, making sure kids have good choice and where their parents have good choice, where their kids are going to go to school and helping our law enforcement.",
